    "h1": "Complete VIN Check Guide: 2017 Genesis G80 Electrified",
    "content": "A Vehicle Identification Number (VIN) serves as a unique legal and technical fingerprint for every automobile. For a 2017 Genesis G80 Electrified registered in Maryland, a meticulous VIN check is a critical antifraud procedure that cross-references engineering data with state title records. This process verifies the vehicle's identity against manufacturer specifications and Maryland DMV documentation to uncover discrepancies that may indicate fraud, previous significant damage, or improper titling. The 17-character VIN `1HGDNP5P3H3241149` is decoded by segment to extract specific identifiers, beginning with the World Manufacturer Identifier (WMI) `1HG`.\n\n*   **Regulatory Compliance Verification:** The check confirms alignment with the **Maryland Vehicle Code**, ensuring the title history reflects accurate branding, such as **Salvage**, **Rebuilt**, **Flood**, or **Junk**, which are permanently recorded in this title-holding state.\n*   **Structural and Safety Data Correlation:** While specific platform data for this model is not detailed in standard reports, the vehicle history.\n\n## VIN Decoder for 2017 Genesis G80 Electrified\n\nA Vehicle Identification Number (VIN) is a unique 17-character code that serves as a legal and technical fingerprint for a vehicle. For a 2017 Genesis G80 Electrified registered in Maryland, decoding this VIN provides the foundational data for verifying the vehicle's specifications and origin against official records. This process is a critical first step in any comprehensive vehicle history check, enabling you to confirm core manufacturing details before investigating title status, accident history, or odometer readings through standard state and federal data sources.\n\n<table><tr><th>Position</th><th>Range</th><th>Meaning</th></tr><tr><td>1-3</td><td>WMI</td><td>World Manufacturer Identifier: 1HG = United States, Honda, Unknown</td></tr><tr><td>4-8</td><td>VDS</td><td>Vehicle Descriptor Section: Model-specific codes for 2017 Genesis G80 Electrified (body style, trim, safety features, engine)</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>Check Digit</td><td>Mathematical validation digit (calculated via NHTSA algorithm)</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>Year</td><td>Model Year: H = 2017</td></tr><tr><td>11</td><td>Plant</td><td>Assembly Plant: [varies by Genesis manufacturing facility]</td></tr><tr><td>12-17</td><td>Serial</td><td>Production Sequence: Unique serial number (from example VIN 1HGDNP5P3H3241149)</td></tr></table>\n\n*   **WMI (Positions 1-3):** The code.\n\n## NMVTIS: National Motor Vehicle Title Information System\n\nA vehicle history report for a 2017 Genesis G80 Electrified in Maryland relies heavily on data from the National Motor Vehicle Title Information System (NMVTIS). This federally mandated system is designed to prevent fraud and protect consumers by creating a centralized record of a vehicle's title history. For a vehicle like the Genesis G80 Electrified, NMVTIS provides a crucial, government-verified audit trail that supplements a standard VIN check. The system aggregates data from mandatory reporting by state titling agencies, insurance carriers, and salvage and junk yards, creating a foundational layer of information that is critical for assessing a vehicle's legal and structural status.\n\nThe procedural value of an NMVTIS report lies in its standardized data points, which allow for systematic verification. When reviewing a report, you should methodically check for the following key entries, which are mandated for reporting to the system:\n\n*   **Title Brand History:** This is the core anti-fraud component. The report will list any brands applied to the vehicle's title according to the **Maryland DMV**. Permissible brands in Maryland include **Salvage**, **Rebuilt**, **Flood**, and **Junk**. A brand is a permanent legal designation of significant past condition.\n*   **Odometer Readings:** NMVTIS requires the disclosure of odometer readings from each title transaction. A discrepancy or rollback in this sequential data is a direct indicator of potential fraud.\n*   **Theft Records:** The system includes data on whether the vehicle has ever been reported as stolen to law enforcement and if that status has been cleared.\n*   **Salvage and Junk Yard Entries:** If the vehicle was ever declared a total loss by an insurance company and sent to a salvage pool, or if it was reported by a junk yard as being dismantled, this event must be recorded in NMVTIS.\n\nFor Maryland residents, it is essential to understand that Maryland operates a **title-holding** system. This means the physical certificate of title is a controlled document held by the lienholder when a loan is active or by the owner if the vehicle is owned outright. The NMVTIS data reflects the official titling actions processed through the **Maryland DMV** under the **Mary.\n\n## Accident Intelligence\n\nA vehicle history report for a 2017 Genesis G80 Electrified in Maryland synthesizes data from standard state and federal data sources to provide a structured assessment of accident-related events. This intelligence is critical for evaluating safety, value, and legal title status, particularly for an electrified vehicle where high-voltage system integrity is paramount. The analysis follows a procedural checklist to identify discrepancies and potential fraud.\n\n*   **Event Categorization:** Reported incidents are classified by severity and type, such as collisions, fire, or hail damage. Each event record is cross-referenced with the vehicle's VIN, `1HGDNP5P3H3241149`, to ensure it pertains specifically to this Genesis. The absence of an event in a report does not guarantee a vehicle is accident-free, as not all incidents are universally reported.\n*   **Title Brand Analysis:** Under the **Maryland Vehicle Code**, the Maryland DMV assigns permanent title brands like **Salvage**, **Rebuilt**, **Flood**, or **Junk** to vehicles that have sustained significant damage. A **Rebuilt** brand indi